The fs (File System) module is a built-in Node.js module used to work with files and directories on your computer. It lets your JavaScript program create, read, update, delete, copy, move, and inspect files.

What fs can do
Read files
Write files
Append data to files
Delete files
Rename or move files
Copy files
Create and remove directories
Read directory contents
Check if files exist
Get file information (size, timestamps, permissions)
Watch files for changes